oir/a-79309465?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Here are some of the key revelations from Charles Earl Spencer's highly anticipated memoir "Swan Song: Diana, My Sister." It has already provoked Buckingham Palace to react.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Police investigate alleged gang-rape in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29df3d5197bbba3fe9c0eeab07e1f06b4cab8cb88629f22f5e2be4d9df0ef5cc</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:31:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T06:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-police-investigate-alleged-gang-rape-in-delhi/live-79365177--41caa0443681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-police-investigate-alleged-gang-rape-in-delhi/live-79365177?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While India is fuming over a viral video of two minors being harassed in Bihar, a case of an alleged gang-rape of a minor has emerged in a posh Delhi neighborhood. Meanwhile, India's foreign minister is at the UNGA.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>G7 demands Houthis 'immediately' cease Saudi strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf7ded6e25b1e3b2d79d621a0da05471626179492824f796f0399ca1544992a5</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:31:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T04:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/g7-demands-houthis-immediately-cease-saudi-strikes/a-79364964--b1476907806f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/g7-demands-houthis-immediately-cease-saudi-strikes/a-79364964?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The G7 nations have accused Yemen's Houthi rebels of targeting civilian shipping near Saudi Arabia. UK PM Andy Burnham said he will offer "time-limited" and "defensive" military support to repel the attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Man charged over suspected role in Rwanda genocide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50d5966818664a2fd7bb2d83b9617b3653aaf9387f817a369120ef7e2333f65e</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T21:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-man-charged-over-suspected-role-in-rwanda-genocide/a-79364493--8067a57ec627.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-man-charged-over-suspected-role-in-rwanda-genocide/a-79364493?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The suspect has been accused of directing and inciting acts of murder and genocide carried out by others in Rwanda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Trump-Xi summit nears, Europe is caught in middle of US-China rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17547ad4e56506c9770fcffa7157b0c177f7ac97cecaa50d0ec6f20a58ebe9d9</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:31:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540--3c6355b77845.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China's Xi Jinping is traveling to Washington this week. Regardless of what comes from his talks with US President Trump, the EU will likely remain stuck between erratic US trade policy and Beijing's export machine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US news outlets sue Trump over White House ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f8eaa374cc3db773ca57e37adea9d6cb17c800584f9482669beef7fb8018dbc</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-news-outlets-sue-trump-over-white-house-ban/a-79362618--679324f34291.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-news-outlets-sue-trump-over-white-house-ban/a-79362618?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CNN, MS NOW, and Politico say the ban against them threatens press freedom and the right to independent journalism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nuclear power is back on Southeast Asia's energy agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:263afdb778e6d38f0580a6c29d42995ec06bab625770265bac054a5a616c7aaf</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744--70fdccf67ff5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising electricity demand, shocks in energy security and climate commitments are reviving long-stalled plans for nuclear power across Southeast Asia. But proponents of nuclear energy still face major obstacles.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why gender-based violence persists in Southern Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c85f90b618f57af7f81e59c556f4e9bd15ff811c5a4ce7a2fb5ab2bf9e749ef</id><updated>2026-09-22T13:29:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T13:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-gender-based-violence-persists-in-southern-africa/a-79356560--3226110a275f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-gender-based-violence-persists-in-southern-africa/a-79356560?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A series of killings in South Africa has renewed scrutiny of efforts to combat violence against women. Activists say laws alone are not enough without effective implementation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's road rage: When cars become weapons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb8c94